{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793681974,"nonce":"bkAINUYzA4mK6v3BSRlkAqZ5le0=","title":"Report helpers: duplicated node-ID lookup and fallback name; outcome wording in the CLI","message":"Found by the M4 code review (maintainability reviewer). Listed under \"Not addressed here\" in https://github.com/icosahedron/csharp-ansatz/pull/1. Parent epic: `54c6e06f383039f9758f1571999c683db1c244561561998cf9a52c41b84fa52f`.\n\nThree small cleanups in untrusted code, best done before M5a's in-process verify and build task start reusing the reports:\n\n- **Duplicated node-ID lookup.** \"A node's ID is its pre-order index\" is implemented twice, as a linear scan in `Pipeline.Sides` and in `AssumptionReports.ClaimSpan` (`src/Warrant.Engine/Reports/AssumptionReport.cs`). Add one helper, for example `VirTree.IdOf`, and use it in both places.\n- **Duplicated fallback name.** `AssumptionReports.FallbackName` duplicates `LeanNames.FallbackDisplay`. Use one.\n- **Outcome wording in the CLI.** The wording for WRT0001 and WRT0006, and the bundle's name and SHA-256, live in `src/Warrant.Cli/TranslateCommand.cs`, while `AssumptionReports` words the same outcomes separately. Move them to `Warrant.Engine`, so M5a's callers do not copy them.\n\nNo behaviour change: the CLI tests and the assumption-report output stay the same.","files":null}]}